1
00:00:27,170 --> 00:00:28,510
(THE YARNS)

2
00:01:12,960 --> 00:01:15,621
Gather the evidence, then arrest the suspect.

3
00:01:16,461 --> 00:01:19,490
Let's prove whether Sky is the real killer or not.

4
00:01:19,752 --> 00:01:21,694
Officer is not Sky's friend

5
00:01:21,858 --> 00:01:25,378
Lock Sky up here. Sky hates the officer.

6
00:01:25,494 --> 00:01:28,592
I want to use the remaining time to prove that we didn't catch the wrong person.

7
00:01:28,650 --> 00:01:30,221
University name?

8
00:01:30,363 --> 00:01:33,007
There will also be an abandoned factory in that area.

9
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:20,760
- Let's go back.
- Alright.

10
00:04:54,021 --> 00:04:55,545
Stop! Stop!

11
00:04:56,007 --> 00:04:56,941
Stop!

12
00:05:01,180 --> 00:05:02,000
Sergeant, hurry up!

13
00:05:02,974 --> 00:05:03,865
Yes, sir.

14
00:05:07,774 --> 00:05:10,072
Hey! Damn it!

15
00:05:10,501 --> 00:05:13,701
Hey, hang in there! I'm a police officer.

16
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:29,687
Ouch!

17
00:06:16,436 --> 00:06:18,858
- Lan, how are you doing?
- Sergeant, how's the victim doing?

18
00:06:21,505 --> 00:06:22,320
He

19
00:06:23,658 --> 00:06:26,818
- He’s deceased.
- The victim can't breathe on their own, Lan.

20
00:06:27,250 --> 00:06:32,236
We tried to cut the threads
around the nose, eyes, and mouth.

21
00:06:32,520 --> 00:06:36,690
We found that the superglue
had sealed all the victim's airways.

22
00:06:36,832 --> 00:06:39,436
So, we couldn't insert any tubes or wires at all.

23
00:06:39,832 --> 00:06:41,541
The victim tried to open their eyes and mouth.

24
00:06:41,847 --> 00:06:48,370
But because of the glue, it only made everything tear apart, leading to death.

25
00:06:49,820 --> 00:06:52,316
The sergeant said you’ve found the real killer, Lan.

26
00:06:53,178 --> 00:06:54,014
Really?

27
00:06:54,650 --> 00:06:55,596
I didn't see their face.

28
00:06:56,440 --> 00:06:58,618
But based on the size, it’s likely the killer is a woman.

29
00:07:00,694 --> 00:07:04,254
So, this means Sky isn't the killer.

30
00:07:05,647 --> 00:07:09,580
Lan, I'm sorry for not believing you back then.

31
00:07:12,520 --> 00:07:13,541
It's okay, An.

32
00:07:14,189 --> 00:07:17,980
Because according to the evidence and forensic principles,
it had to be the way you thought, An.

33
00:07:22,705 --> 00:07:23,560
Sergeant.

34
00:07:24,680 --> 00:07:25,581
Please help me.

35
00:07:26,309 --> 00:07:27,160
Alright.

36
00:07:33,200 --> 00:07:38,080
The plaintiff's evidence carries more weight than the defendant's evidence.

37
00:07:38,360 --> 00:07:44,432
The facts presented are sufficient to conclude that the defendant is guilty under the Penal Code.

38
00:07:44,560 --> 00:07:47,174
Section 289 (4)

39
00:07:47,414 --> 00:07:49,854
Premeditated murder

40
00:07:50,323 --> 00:07:52,709
Section 289 (5)

41
00:07:53,138 --> 00:07:55,221
Murders another person by employing torture

42
00:07:55,338 --> 00:07:58,992
or acts of cruelty, shall be punished.

43
00:08:00,665 --> 00:08:01,829
May I please, Your Honor?

44
00:08:02,400 --> 00:08:06,960
The court is now rendering its judgment in this case. According to Section 198 of the Penal Code

45
00:08:07,076 --> 00:08:10,596
Whoever obstructs the examination
or judgment of the court

46
00:08:10,741 --> 00:08:12,880
shall be punishable by imprisonment
from one to seven years,

47
00:08:12,912 --> 00:08:16,494
or a fine from 40,000 to 120,000 baht,
or both imprisonment and fine.

48
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:17,980
With respect,

49
00:08:18,792 --> 00:08:20,745
I am Police Lieutenant Colonel Pilanthorn Traikanon.

50
00:08:21,367 --> 00:08:23,545
Head of the Special Investigation Unit for Serial Murder Cases.

51
00:08:23,850 --> 00:08:25,901
There are certain matters that the court needs to be aware of

52
00:08:26,207 --> 00:08:27,716
Before the judgment is read.

53
00:08:34,200 --> 00:08:36,440
The judgment will be recessed for 30 minutes.

54
00:08:45,694 --> 00:08:47,549
How is the witness sure that

55
00:08:47,796 --> 00:08:50,763
the person they encountered is the real criminal?

56
00:08:51,298 --> 00:08:52,316
In this case,

57
00:08:52,723 --> 00:08:54,752
the perpetrator leaves a scarf on each victim's body.

58
00:08:55,180 --> 00:08:56,523
This body is the same.

59
00:08:57,098 --> 00:08:58,396
Just a knitted scarf.

60
00:08:58,963 --> 00:09:01,098
How can we confirm who the killer is?

61
00:09:01,258 --> 00:09:05,083
then anyone who can knit a scarf
would be considered the criminal.

62
00:09:07,029 --> 00:09:09,850
Each scarf will have a mystery hidden within it.

63
00:09:10,185 --> 00:09:14,556
The mystery will reveal the occupation of the next victim, along with the clue on the most recent scarf.

64
00:09:15,356 --> 00:09:19,280
The occupation mentioned is a student,
and the victim is a student.

65
00:09:19,603 --> 00:09:24,763
This answer is known only to me
and Police Major Damrong Tangsamyuth.

66
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:33,032
You fought with the criminal, didn't you?

67
00:09:34,480 --> 00:09:35,476
Yes, sir.

68
00:09:37,672 --> 00:09:40,741
And this is the weapon the criminal used in the fight

69
00:09:40,800 --> 00:09:42,407
and harmed you, didn't they?

70
00:09:42,509 --> 00:09:43,487
Yes, sir.

71
00:09:50,410 --> 00:09:53,705
You were the prison officer with the defendant on the night of the incident, weren't you?

72
00:09:53,843 --> 00:09:54,654
Yes.

73
00:09:55,520 --> 00:09:56,687
According to the testimony,

74
00:09:56,941 --> 00:09:58,014
on the night of the incident,

75
00:09:58,301 --> 00:09:59,920
the defendant was delirious.

76
00:10:00,127 --> 00:10:03,425
Could you tell me

77
00:10:03,461 --> 00:10:04,323
what happened that night?

78
00:10:04,541 --> 00:10:05,425
Yes.

79
00:10:05,880 --> 00:10:11,127
Suddenly, the defendant shouting and repeatedly saying, I have to go, I have to go,

80
00:10:11,527 --> 00:10:14,210
someone is going to die, saying it over and over.

81
00:10:14,349 --> 00:10:16,254
I have to go, Sky has to go.

82
00:10:16,316 --> 00:10:18,349
Someone is going to die! Someone is going to die!

83
00:10:18,741 --> 00:10:19,712
Sky has to go

84
00:10:19,843 --> 00:10:20,920
Someone is going to die!

85
00:10:21,243 --> 00:10:22,825
- Someone is going to die!
- Where are you going?

86
00:10:22,985 --> 00:10:25,640
- Nurse, call the nurse.
- Someone is going to die! Let Sky go.

87
00:10:25,680 --> 00:10:28,229
- Let Sky go. Sky has to go.
- Calm down. Calm down.

88
00:10:28,305 --> 00:10:30,469
-Sky has to go. Has to go right now.
-Stay calm.

89
00:10:30,578 --> 00:10:34,232
- Calm down. Call the nurse.
- Someone is going to die! Someone is going to die!

90
00:10:34,320 --> 00:10:36,960
But suddenly, the defendant became calm

91
00:10:37,301 --> 00:10:38,665
and asked for a scarf,

92
00:10:38,756 --> 00:10:41,054
knitting needles, or a crochet hook.

93
00:10:41,203 --> 00:10:44,294
But by law, I couldn't give it, so I didn't.

94
00:10:46,600 --> 00:10:47,894
No further questions.

95
00:10:49,180 --> 00:10:54,756
According to the results of the autopsy
of Miss Oratchuma Sapleksakun, the eighth victim.

96
00:10:55,880 --> 00:11:00,098
There are specific characteristics that align with
the seven previous murders.

97
00:11:00,381 --> 00:11:03,549
The criminal is likely the same person.

98
00:11:08,480 --> 00:11:09,661
No further questions.

99
00:11:13,730 --> 00:11:17,240
- Mom
- Sky, Sky

100
00:11:17,360 --> 00:11:18,101
Sky

101
00:11:18,272 --> 00:11:22,978
Sky, May God bless you, my child.

102
00:11:43,996 --> 00:11:46,287
Mom, Sky can't breathe.

103
00:11:47,163 --> 00:11:49,265
Mom, you're hugging so tightly.

104
00:11:49,301 --> 00:11:52,283
God bless you.

105
00:11:53,454 --> 00:11:54,596
Mom is so happy.

106
00:11:57,050 --> 00:11:59,767
Sky... you don't hate me anymore, right?

107
00:12:07,087 --> 00:12:10,927
Mom, Sky wants to go home.
Please take me back home.

108
00:12:11,174 --> 00:12:14,796
Sky wants to go back and knit scarves.
Please take me home, Mom.

109
00:12:15,872 --> 00:12:19,076
Let's go home. I ordered your favorite Thai rice noodles for you.

110
00:12:19,774 --> 00:12:20,974
-Let's go.
-Let's head back.

111
00:12:22,370 --> 00:12:24,032
Excuse me, officer.

112
00:12:27,250 --> 00:12:30,927
Thank you for helping me and my daughter.

113
00:12:32,880 --> 00:12:33,763
It's no problem at all.

114
00:12:34,140 --> 00:12:35,552
It's my duty.

115
00:12:35,698 --> 00:12:39,192
But I do want to thank the court
for listening to our explanation.

116
00:12:41,752 --> 00:12:42,596
I'll take you.

117
00:12:57,580 --> 00:12:59,225
The court has granted bail.

118
00:12:59,505 --> 00:13:01,640
You must feel a little more at ease now.

119
00:13:02,840 --> 00:13:06,523
I have to thank the inspector
and everyone else who helped us.

120
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:07,901
Thank you so much.

121
00:13:08,214 --> 00:13:11,792
Oh, and I should also apologize to Sergeant Moo for what happened earlier.

122
00:13:13,180 --> 00:13:16,123
I must apologize to you too, Miss Sookwan

123
00:13:16,414 --> 00:13:19,290
- I lost my composure back then.
- It's alright.

124
00:13:20,072 --> 00:13:22,018
What will happen next?

125
00:13:23,316 --> 00:13:25,967
The police will have to catch the real criminal.

126
00:13:27,469 --> 00:13:28,414
Please take care of that.

127
00:13:34,181 --> 00:13:35,821
Sky, eat this.

128
00:13:37,956 --> 00:13:41,203
- What is this, Mark?
- Tofu.

129
00:13:42,065 --> 00:13:44,880
- Why does Sky have to eat tofu?
- Huh?

130
00:13:45,480 --> 00:13:49,290
Haven't you watched Korean dramas? When someone is acquitted, they have to eat tofu.

131
00:13:49,490 --> 00:13:51,265
What is Korean?

132
00:13:52,560 --> 00:13:53,727
Silly.

133
00:13:54,210 --> 00:13:59,600
-According to Chinese tradition, it's supposed to be pomelo and boiled eggs.
-Oh, Sergeant.

134
00:14:00,480 --> 00:14:01,378
I don't eat it.

135
00:14:01,520 --> 00:14:04,374
There's only stuff I don't like.
Why do I have to eat it?

136
00:14:05,563 --> 00:14:07,505
Then, as a Thai person, we have to

137
00:14:08,476 --> 00:14:10,780
This... You have to take a bath.

138
00:14:12,065 --> 00:14:12,865
Holy water.

139
00:14:13,487 --> 00:14:16,203
No... I don't want to. I won't bathe, Mom.

140
00:14:16,454 --> 00:14:20,640
Let’s eat Khanom Jeen instead,
before the food gets cold.

141
00:14:20,680 --> 00:14:22,120
Yes, let's eat.

142
00:14:23,563 --> 00:14:24,585
Oops, Sergeant.

143
00:14:25,403 --> 00:14:26,701
How did you take it from me?

144
00:14:27,156 --> 00:14:29,483
Alright, eat it with the noodles then.

145
00:14:29,520 --> 00:14:31,407
Sergeant, you can eat first.

146
00:14:31,461 --> 00:14:32,650
Thank you.

147
00:15:21,101 --> 00:15:22,701
What are you doing sitting here?

148
00:15:23,040 --> 00:15:23,720
Why?

149
00:15:25,927 --> 00:15:28,163
Do I look that desperate?

150
00:15:40,814 --> 00:15:42,149
So, what are you hoping for?

151
00:15:45,200 --> 00:15:46,570
Don’t I have the right to hope?

152
00:15:47,392 --> 00:15:50,301
As long as Lan isn’t with anyone, I think I have the right.

153
00:16:05,723 --> 00:16:06,520
What about me?

154
00:16:09,650 --> 00:16:10,723
Do I still have the right to hope?

155
00:16:14,400 --> 00:16:15,647
Because you’re still alone.

156
00:16:21,120 --> 00:16:22,780
Can I be the one?

157
00:16:23,600 --> 00:16:24,290
Why?

158
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:28,265
Are you going to be my fork?

159
00:16:34,509 --> 00:16:35,600
Did you hear that?

160
00:16:40,294 --> 00:16:41,229
Thank you.

161
00:16:41,301 --> 00:16:43,818
That night, you didn't offend me when I was drunk.

162
00:16:44,818 --> 00:16:46,098
Since we met,

163
00:16:46,621 --> 00:16:48,636
That night, you were really such a great guy.

164
00:16:54,327 --> 00:16:55,040
I’m going now.

165
00:17:04,189 --> 00:17:04,883
Thanks.

166
00:17:05,585 --> 00:17:06,185
Okay.

167
00:17:43,869 --> 00:17:47,025
An, Let’s go home. Go home. An.

168
00:17:47,930 --> 00:17:49,610
Bro. Bro.

169
00:17:50,683 --> 00:17:51,538
Check please.

170
00:17:55,723 --> 00:17:56,760
Let’s go home.

171
00:18:08,400 --> 00:18:08,981
Yes. Sir.

172
00:18:23,980 --> 00:18:27,505
You look really troubled,
even came to see me in person

173
00:18:27,629 --> 00:18:28,780
instead of just calling.

174
00:18:29,454 --> 00:18:31,061
With all the criticism,

175
00:18:31,505 --> 00:18:32,774
I would be worried.

176
00:18:34,967 --> 00:18:36,752
But I’m more concerned about the people

177
00:18:37,338 --> 00:18:41,705
who have to live without safety because the police like you are ineffective.

178
00:18:42,130 --> 00:18:43,614
Why don't you ask your son

179
00:18:44,210 --> 00:18:45,280
how he works?

180
00:18:45,800 --> 00:18:47,418
Why are the police being criticized like this?

181
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:54,476
My son is just a subordinate.
If you want to hold someone accountable,

182
00:18:55,218 --> 00:18:57,941
you should ask his superior.

183
00:18:58,556 --> 00:19:01,832
The police are so confident that they have caught the criminal.

184
00:19:02,530 --> 00:19:04,076
Why are there still new victims?

185
00:19:05,200 --> 00:19:07,403
Okay, I admit my mistakes.

186
00:19:08,181 --> 00:19:11,250
If there's a demand for accountability, I'm ready to resign.

187
00:19:13,065 --> 00:19:13,967
But what about you?

188
00:19:14,596 --> 00:19:15,400
Are you ready

189
00:19:15,938 --> 00:19:18,498
to withdraw from the race for the mayor's seat

190
00:19:18,560 --> 00:19:19,476
that you desire?

191
00:19:37,960 --> 00:19:38,752
Dad

192
00:19:40,130 --> 00:19:42,832
You came to see me here.
Is there something important?

193
00:19:44,229 --> 00:19:45,512
I'm here

194
00:19:46,312 --> 00:19:47,687
to tell you that

195
00:19:48,389 --> 00:19:50,490
you should quit your job.

196
00:19:50,800 --> 00:19:52,578
How many more people are you going to let die?

197
00:19:57,840 --> 00:20:01,356
Have you ever thought about the feelings of the people
who lost because of your terrible work?

198
00:20:01,760 --> 00:20:03,527
Because of your incompetence!

199
00:20:04,094 --> 00:20:06,221
But the inspector has tried his best.

200
00:20:06,440 --> 00:20:11,254
He even sacrificed himself to catch the criminal.

201
00:20:13,389 --> 00:20:14,734
Is this your best?

202
00:20:16,472 --> 00:20:18,349
Just for one psychotic killer?

203
00:20:18,523 --> 00:20:21,916
The entire police department
still hasn't been able to catch him.

204
00:20:27,138 --> 00:20:28,349
And like this,

205
00:20:29,320 --> 00:20:31,323
who can the people rely on?

206
00:20:42,556 --> 00:20:44,938
You must solve this case before the election.

207
00:20:46,640 --> 00:20:48,403
And it must go as I expect.

208
00:20:54,963 --> 00:20:56,076
And I hope this time

209
00:20:57,869 --> 00:21:00,450
you won't disappoint me, right?

210
00:21:21,580 --> 00:21:23,174
Take care of my son.

211
00:21:26,120 --> 00:21:28,007
And if he does something wrong,

212
00:21:29,240 --> 00:21:30,760
feel free to reprimand him.

213
00:21:36,581 --> 00:21:37,920
Don't think of him as my son.

214
00:22:09,814 --> 00:22:11,443
It's binary, right Sky?

215
00:22:12,563 --> 00:22:14,000
It seems like there are two sets.

216
00:22:14,061 --> 00:22:15,760
We tried decoding it before.

217
00:22:15,792 --> 00:22:17,872
It looked like we got letters, but they didn’t form words.

218
00:22:20,570 --> 00:22:23,010
Yes, it’s really in binary code.

219
00:22:23,738 --> 00:22:26,032
Followed by two sets that are connected like this.

220
00:22:26,258 --> 00:22:27,389
It should be...

221
00:22:31,574 --> 00:22:33,447
Yes, definitely.

222
00:22:33,680 --> 00:22:35,980
What’s that? Sky, tell us.

223
00:22:36,429 --> 00:22:37,967
It’s an ASCII code.

224
00:22:39,847 --> 00:22:40,890
What code again?

225
00:22:41,265 --> 00:22:42,265
ASCII

226
00:22:42,512 --> 00:22:43,774
ASCII

227
00:22:43,880 --> 00:22:46,963
or American Standard Code for Information Interchange

228
00:22:47,083 --> 00:22:49,210
It’s commonly used by computer creators.

229
00:22:49,280 --> 00:22:52,818
It’s a character code
consisting of Latin letters, Arabic numerals,

230
00:22:52,923 --> 00:22:54,927
punctuation marks, and various symbols.

231
00:22:55,043 --> 00:22:57,927
Each code represents a character.

232
00:22:58,000 --> 00:22:59,025
For example, code 65

233
00:22:59,076 --> 00:23:00,032
in decimal

234
00:23:00,163 --> 00:23:02,112
represents the capital letter A.

235
00:23:05,654 --> 00:23:09,600
Can you explain it simply and tell us how to decode it?

236
00:23:09,887 --> 00:23:11,560
ASCII can be written in 3 ways.

237
00:23:11,705 --> 00:23:13,956
Decimal, binary, and hexadecimal.

238
00:23:14,320 --> 00:23:16,214
It should be converted to character values.

239
00:23:16,298 --> 00:23:18,109
This time, it's in binary code.

240
00:23:18,160 --> 00:23:20,778
You need to replace the values
with characters from the table.

241
00:23:21,207 --> 00:23:22,185
Table?

242
00:23:23,298 --> 00:23:25,283
Here it is, the schedule that Sky mentioned.

243
00:23:26,730 --> 00:23:27,580
Right?

244
00:23:28,730 --> 00:23:30,952
Yes, that’s correct, Doctor Anya.

245
00:23:31,180 --> 00:23:31,938
Expand it a bit.

246
00:23:34,596 --> 00:23:36,050
What’s next, Sky?

247
00:23:37,830 --> 00:23:42,483
Two sets of binary. One vertical, one horizontal, but...

248
00:23:44,280 --> 00:23:45,007
Uh...

249
00:23:46,389 --> 00:23:47,010
What?

250
00:23:48,069 --> 00:23:51,636
Sky isn’t sure which set the killer assigned as vertical

251
00:23:51,680 --> 00:23:52,996
and which as horizontal.

252
00:23:53,232 --> 00:23:54,269
Sky don’t know.

253
00:23:54,669 --> 00:23:55,821
Does anyone know?

254
00:23:58,563 --> 00:24:01,032
If we knew, would we call Sky for help.

255
00:24:01,647 --> 00:24:02,596
Yes, quite so.

256
00:24:03,229 --> 00:24:06,076
Because Sky is good. Mom says Sky is good.

257
00:24:06,480 --> 00:24:10,243
It’s simple. If we want the answer,
we need to try both ways.

258
00:24:12,145 --> 00:24:12,963
Both ways?

259
00:24:13,647 --> 00:24:15,480
Let’s start then.

260
00:24:17,007 --> 00:24:20,436
Let’s try the first set as vertical
and the second as horizontal.

261
00:24:20,570 --> 00:24:21,127
Okay.

262
00:24:21,469 --> 00:24:24,498
Then, Sky and I will read the code, Mark and Anya.

