The child was abandoned under a banyan tree near a temple around Nonthaburi.

517
00:42:11,370 --> 00:42:13,385
A man was the one who abandoned the child there.

518
00:42:13,694 --> 00:42:18,512
The man wasn't careful when
crossing the street and got hit by a car,

519
00:42:18,665 --> 00:42:20,949
dying before he could do anything. The driver who hit him reported the incident.

520
00:42:21,283 --> 00:42:24,581
The police then coordinated with us to take the child.

521
00:42:25,698 --> 00:42:27,800
Someone abandoned Sky?

522
00:42:28,669 --> 00:42:30,800
Someone really abandoned Sky

523
00:42:31,072 --> 00:42:31,869
Sky.

524
00:42:37,138 --> 00:42:40,734
The person who died had
clear identification documents,

525
00:42:40,872 --> 00:42:46,258
but by the time the police investigated,
they had already moved away.

526
00:42:46,698 --> 00:42:49,421
Here are the documents you requested.

527
00:42:49,534 --> 00:42:50,141
Thank you.

528
00:42:50,472 --> 00:42:53,007
Was there only one child that day?

529
00:42:53,440 --> 00:42:53,854
Yes.

530
00:42:54,265 --> 00:42:56,840
There was only one child. Is something wrong?

531
00:42:57,465 --> 00:42:58,414
No, nothing.

532
00:42:59,585 --> 00:43:02,309
- Thank you so much.
- I’ll take my leave now.

533
00:43:18,080 --> 00:43:19,800
Mr. Bancha Sanguankhun.

534
00:43:21,392 --> 00:43:25,021
The other children were also abandoned like Sky, right?

535
00:43:33,410 --> 00:43:34,912
But Sky is very lucky

536
00:43:35,920 --> 00:43:37,636
that Sukhwan took Sky in.

537
00:43:39,520 --> 00:43:40,189
Yes.

538
00:43:40,865 --> 00:43:43,520
Sky is fortunate to have been adopted by a mom.

539
00:43:50,556 --> 00:43:53,614
I hope the other children are as lucky as Sky.

540
00:43:54,800 --> 00:43:55,912
Stay strong.

541
00:44:04,894 --> 00:44:06,850
Let's go, Sky.

542
00:44:07,600 --> 00:44:08,672
Where are we going?

543
00:44:09,250 --> 00:44:14,687
We’re going to find the person who abandoned Sky.
But the staff said they’ve all moved already.

544
00:44:15,580 --> 00:44:20,047
But isn't it better than just sitting and doing nothing?

545
00:44:44,276 --> 00:44:47,534
Excuse me, have you seen the person in this photo?

546
00:44:50,240 --> 00:44:50,843
No, I haven’t.

547
00:44:51,923 --> 00:44:52,676
Thank you.

548
00:45:06,654 --> 00:45:07,970
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

549
00:45:08,340 --> 00:45:09,669
Have you seen the person in this photo?

550
00:45:09,749 --> 00:45:12,760
- I’ve never seen him.
- Okay

551
00:45:13,180 --> 00:45:14,912
- It's okay, thank you.
- You're welcome.

552
00:45:16,072 --> 00:45:16,780
Excuse me.

553
00:45:17,196 --> 00:45:19,632
Excuse me, have you ever seen the person in this photo?

554
00:45:20,545 --> 00:45:22,661
- No, I haven't.
- Alright, thank you.

555
00:45:29,556 --> 00:45:30,309
Excuse me.

556
00:45:30,596 --> 00:45:31,767
Have you ever seen the person in this photo?

557
00:45:33,901 --> 00:45:35,745
No, I haven’t. I just moved here.

558
00:45:35,980 --> 00:45:37,301
Try asking inside.

559
00:45:38,083 --> 00:45:38,869
Thank you so much.

560
00:46:00,130 --> 00:46:01,636
Sorry, excuse me.

561
00:46:02,647 --> 00:46:04,483
Have you ever seen the person in this photo?

562
00:46:05,185 --> 00:46:05,980
I’ve never seen them.

563
00:46:07,221 --> 00:46:08,029
Thank you.

564
00:46:15,520 --> 00:46:16,210
Excuse me.

565
00:46:17,087 --> 00:46:18,410
Have you ever seen the person in this photo?

566
00:46:20,774 --> 00:46:21,614
No, I haven’t.

567
00:46:22,625 --> 00:46:23,305
Thank you.

568
00:46:28,145 --> 00:46:30,781
Hello, have you ever seen the person in this photo?

569
00:46:32,516 --> 00:46:33,283
Don’t know anything about this person.

570
00:46:44,501 --> 00:46:45,152
Sky

571
00:46:45,763 --> 00:46:47,032
How about we take a break and have some water?

572
00:46:47,570 --> 00:46:48,694
Your face is all red.

573
00:46:50,247 --> 00:46:51,709
- Is my face red?
- Yes.

574
00:46:51,985 --> 00:46:53,803
Is my face really red?

575
00:46:54,145 --> 00:46:56,410
I’m not embarrassed by the police.

576
00:46:57,145 --> 00:46:58,705
I didn’t mean you’re embarrassed.

577
00:46:59,174 --> 00:47:00,400
I meant Sky feels hot.

578
00:47:01,127 --> 00:47:02,058
Oh, I see.

579
00:47:03,105 --> 00:47:03,774
Yes.

580
00:47:06,145 --> 00:47:07,621
Auntie, two bottles of water, please.

581
00:47:08,832 --> 00:47:10,105
Alright, just a moment.

582
00:47:10,780 --> 00:47:11,680
Make sure they're cold.

583
00:47:11,770 --> 00:47:12,640
Okay.

584
00:47:14,436 --> 00:47:20,883
Officer, will we be able to find the man
who abandoned Sky today?

585
00:47:21,887 --> 00:47:23,229
I'm not sure either.

586
00:47:24,650 --> 00:47:25,694
Sky, are you tired yet?

587
00:47:28,207 --> 00:47:30,298
If not, let's keep looking.

588
00:47:33,774 --> 00:47:35,705
- Here's your water, dear.
- Okay, thank you.

589
00:47:36,934 --> 00:47:37,625
Thank you.

590
00:47:39,240 --> 00:47:41,980
Have you ever seen the person in this photo?

591
00:47:44,810 --> 00:47:45,923
Oh!

592
00:47:46,370 --> 00:47:47,578
Buncha.

593
00:47:47,716 --> 00:47:50,578
Of course, I know him! We were really close. Back then,

594
00:47:50,836 --> 00:47:52,010
Bancha

595
00:47:52,334 --> 00:47:55,650
He used to run a laundry service.
He rented a house from me.

596
00:47:55,920 --> 00:48:00,640
Seeing Bancha reminds me of Duang.

597
00:48:01,211 --> 00:48:03,154
Duang? Who’s that?

598
00:48:03,489 --> 00:48:06,396
Duangjai, Bancha’s wife.

599
00:48:06,510 --> 00:48:10,360
Duang was a talkative and lively person.

600
00:48:10,537 --> 00:48:13,920
I used to stop by and chat with her every day.

601
00:48:17,066 --> 00:48:18,160
Bancha

602
00:48:18,259 --> 00:48:21,215
- Is Duang home?
- Yes, she is. Duang!

603
00:48:21,611 --> 00:48:22,742
Hong is here to see you.

604
00:48:22,899 --> 00:48:24,792
Oh! Where have you been?
Yeah.

605
00:48:24,960 --> 00:48:28,396
- I just came to see you.
- I'm right here, Hong.

606
00:48:28,780 --> 00:48:32,240
Here, take these clothes and hang them up.
Okay. Why are you still holding them?

607
00:48:32,320 --> 00:48:35,900
Exactly! So, tell me now who's the gossip about today?

608
00:48:36,090 --> 00:48:38,209
No need for a long introduction.

609
00:48:38,293 --> 00:48:39,980
Oh. Duang.

610
00:48:40,280 --> 00:48:42,396
You always see right through me.
I can’t hide anything from you!

611
00:48:43,070 --> 00:48:44,460
Come on.

612
00:48:44,819 --> 00:48:46,232
Not just Duang,

613
00:48:46,320 --> 00:48:49,120
even I can tell. I know exactly why you're here.

614
00:48:50,034 --> 00:48:52,840
You and your husband are just the same!

615
00:48:54,780 --> 00:48:56,360
- What?
- What's that smell?

616
00:48:58,198 --> 00:49:00,076
Smells so good! Duang

617
00:49:00,483 --> 00:49:01,725
What are you cooking today?

618
00:49:02,121 --> 00:49:04,982
Gaeng Moo Chamuang Anna’s favorite!

619
00:49:05,462 --> 00:49:08,434
Anna just landed a big job at a major company.

620
00:49:08,537 --> 00:49:09,043
Yeah.

621
00:49:09,093 --> 00:49:10,120
Oh wow,

622
00:49:10,390 --> 00:49:13,386
I’m so happy for her. She’s beautiful,

623
00:49:13,440 --> 00:49:16,575
smart, hardworking, and has such a great personality.

624
00:49:16,906 --> 00:49:20,845
If my kid had even half of Anna’s qualities,

625
00:49:21,238 --> 00:49:25,440
I wouldn’t be hanging around here
gossiping! Anna, your daughter

626
00:49:25,500 --> 00:49:28,280
is truly a gift from heaven.

627
00:49:28,320 --> 00:49:29,790
What are you gossiping about me now, Aunt Hong?

628
00:49:29,862 --> 00:49:30,864
There she is!

629
00:49:32,080 --> 00:49:33,040
Hello.

630
00:49:33,497 --> 00:49:34,780
Hello, dear.
Hello, my child.

631
00:49:35,000 --> 00:49:39,310
I wasn’t gossiping about you!
I was just praising you to your parents.

632
00:49:40,262 --> 00:49:41,127
Anna,

633
00:49:41,321 --> 00:49:42,316
it’s great that you’re here.

634
00:49:42,560 --> 00:49:44,457
I’ll come back to chat another time.

635
00:49:44,480 --> 00:49:48,640
I don’t want to be a third wheel.
You should celebrate together.

636
00:49:48,880 --> 00:49:49,798
I’ll be on my way.

637
00:49:49,960 --> 00:49:51,211
Wait a moment!

638
00:49:51,283 --> 00:49:52,742
Stay and eat with us, Auntie.

639
00:49:52,820 --> 00:49:55,123
- We’re all like family, aren’t we?
- That’s right!

640
00:49:55,180 --> 00:49:57,523
Anna is right. Let’s eat together.

641
00:49:57,641 --> 00:49:59,059
Celebrate

642
00:49:59,240 --> 00:50:01,740
while gossiping about others too, fun as hell!

643
00:50:02,213 --> 00:50:03,800
But is that a good idea?

644
00:50:04,280 --> 00:50:06,120
Oh my, oh my!

645
00:50:07,040 --> 00:50:09,817
Alright then, let’s have we prepare
the meal for Auntie Hong.

646
00:50:09,973 --> 00:50:11,375
I’ll take care of the laundry.

647
00:50:11,500 --> 00:50:12,316
Oh no, no need for that!

648
00:50:12,360 --> 00:50:15,249
You’ve just come home from work,
you must be tired. Go and rest.

649
00:50:15,280 --> 00:50:16,960
- Go and rest. We’ll handle it.
- Mom.

650
00:50:17,120 --> 00:50:19,878
It’s actually mom and dad who should rest!
I’m not tired at all.

651
00:50:20,840 --> 00:50:22,864
Dad's been complaining
about his back pain,hasn't he? Go on.

652
00:50:22,944 --> 00:50:24,179
Yeah, it's still bothering me.

653
00:50:24,228 --> 00:50:27,744
Hey, let the kids be, alright?
Alright, let’s go inside the house.

654
00:50:28,000 --> 00:50:30,636
- Here, come on.
- Let’s go.

655
00:50:30,680 --> 00:50:33,508
- Your daughter Anna is really cute.
- Well,

656
00:50:33,580 --> 00:50:34,270
Come on.

657
00:50:34,330 --> 00:50:37,474
if my kid were like yours,
just half of what yours is.

658
00:50:44,182 --> 00:50:46,620
But who knows what karma brought.

659
00:50:47,085 --> 00:50:49,036
What happened after that?

660
00:50:49,615 --> 00:50:51,535
I don't know either, dear.

661
00:50:52,007 --> 00:50:52,998
Out of nowhere,

662
00:50:53,455 --> 00:50:56,952
Anna went into a frenzy
and shut herself up in the house.

663
00:50:57,379 --> 00:51:02,697
She suddenly screamed so loudly
it echoed to the end of the alley.

664
00:51:03,108 --> 00:51:05,299
You know, people around here

665
00:51:05,493 --> 00:51:09,794
They rumor that Anna was possessed,
but not long after that...

666
00:51:10,403 --> 00:51:12,331
The three of them

667
00:51:13,257 --> 00:51:15,169
just quietly moved out.

668
00:51:15,706 --> 00:51:17,847
Moved? Do you know where they went?

669
00:51:28,120 --> 00:51:29,043
Thank you so much.

670
00:51:45,645 --> 00:51:47,763
What the hell are you reading for?

671
00:52:00,022 --> 00:52:02,281
Even if you're the smartest person in the world,

672
00:52:02,342 --> 00:52:04,327
you'll never become a doctor, Fah.

673
00:52:05,180 --> 00:52:07,443
Come on, help me make keychains. Hurry up.

674
00:52:09,687 --> 00:52:11,866
If it’s not today, one day you’ll make it.

675
00:52:14,342 --> 00:52:16,019
Wake up, Fah.

676
00:52:17,447 --> 00:52:18,495
Someone like you?

677
00:52:18,822 --> 00:52:21,215
Getting a job as a hospital assistant

678
00:52:21,360 --> 00:52:23,920
is already beyond your dreams, Fah.

679
00:52:28,975 --> 00:52:29,535
What?

680
00:52:30,228 --> 00:52:31,710
Where are you going?

681
00:52:33,127 --> 00:52:36,285
Oh, whatever. It’s like talking to a cow or a buffalo.

682
00:52:36,506 --> 00:52:38,316
Go wherever you want,

683
00:52:38,849 --> 00:52:42,853
but just be careful. Lately,
there’ve been reports of several murders.

684
00:52:43,127 --> 00:52:44,533
Do you know about that?

685
00:53:28,438 --> 00:53:29,565
Excuse me, sir.

686
00:53:29,817 --> 00:53:30,167
Yes

687
00:53:30,200 --> 00:53:32,167
Have you ever seen the person in this picture?

688
00:53:33,000 --> 00:53:33,760
No, I haven’t.

689
00:53:34,601 --> 00:53:35,489
Thank you.

690
00:53:46,708 --> 00:53:49,280
Have you ever seen this man? This one right here.

691
00:53:49,424 --> 00:53:50,857
No, I haven’t.

692
00:53:51,100 --> 00:53:52,674
No, I haven’t seen him either.

693
00:53:53,676 --> 00:53:55,160
- Alright, thank you.
- Yes.

694
00:53:58,685 --> 00:53:59,960
Do you know Mr. Bancha

695
00:54:00,152 --> 00:54:03,268
Miss. Duangjai, Anna, or Sky’s twin?

696
00:54:05,592 --> 00:54:08,308
But we came here just like Aunt Hong told us.

697
00:54:09,420 --> 00:54:10,262
Yes, Sky.

698
00:54:10,746 --> 00:54:14,121
We came here just like Aunt Hong said,
but this area is really big, Sky.

699
00:54:14,860 --> 00:54:18,419
Sky tried searching everyone’s name on Google, but there’s no information at all.

700
00:54:18,773 --> 00:54:19,687
Nothing at all.

701
00:54:21,234 --> 00:54:22,967
Should we go to the next alley?

702
00:54:24,480 --> 00:54:24,979
Let’s go.

703
00:54:35,786 --> 00:54:36,495
Hey, wait.

704
00:54:38,849 --> 00:54:40,780
Hey, go ahead, wait.

705
00:54:47,828 --> 00:54:48,422
Wait a minute.

706
00:54:49,080 --> 00:54:49,706
What are you going to do?

707
00:54:54,064 --> 00:54:56,380
Oh, it’s really you, I remember you now.

708
00:54:58,400 --> 00:54:59,211
Sky.

709
00:54:59,725 --> 00:55:01,131
Sky, do you know this man?

710
00:55:02,411 --> 00:55:05,638
I don’t know him, Sky doesn’t know this man.

711
00:55:06,880 --> 00:55:09,036
Oh, really? How could you not know?

712
00:55:09,257 --> 00:55:12,769
It was at the boxing camp that day.
You even asked me to call Nop to come to see you.

713
00:55:13,268 --> 00:55:14,807
Then you both disappeared for the whole night.

714
00:55:15,287 --> 00:55:16,643
When we saw each other again, he was already dead.

715
00:55:16,948 --> 00:55:17,775
Wait a minute.

716
00:55:18,205 --> 00:55:21,043
Is Nop the boxer named Nopchai Songklongla,

717
00:55:21,120 --> 00:55:22,720
the victim of the serial killer?

718
00:55:23,295 --> 00:55:25,055
Yeah, that’s right.

719
00:55:26,285 --> 00:55:32,118
You said your friend, Nopchai,
went with a woman who looked like this?

720
00:55:32,746 --> 00:55:34,102
Yes, it’s this woman.

721
00:55:34,449 --> 00:55:36,060
They said the killer has already been caught.

722
00:55:36,280 --> 00:55:37,649
How is she walking around here?

723
00:55:37,992 --> 00:55:39,424
It’s not Sky.

724
00:55:39,640 --> 00:55:42,750
Sky doesn’t know Mr. Nop, and Sky is not the killer.

725
00:55:43,028 --> 00:55:44,780
Sky, it’s okay.

726
00:55:46,080 --> 00:55:47,000
Let me ask you something.

727
00:55:47,824 --> 00:55:49,729
Did Nopchai and that woman
know each other for a long time?

728
00:55:50,232 --> 00:55:52,369
She's standing here.
Why don't you ask her yourself?

729
00:55:53,400 --> 00:55:54,628
Just answer my question.

730
00:55:56,400 --> 00:55:59,786
Acting all tough, are you a police officer?

731
00:56:08,590 --> 00:56:11,320
Have you answered if those two have known
each other for a long time?

732
00:56:12,308 --> 00:56:13,080
It's not been long.

733
00:56:13,450 --> 00:56:14,560
That day was the first day.

734
00:56:14,792 --> 00:56:16,502
Actually, Nop didn’t want to go.

735
00:56:16,582 --> 00:56:18,392
He was afraid his father would find out
that he skipped practice.

736
00:56:18,834 --> 00:56:20,605
His father owns the boxing camp.

737
00:56:21,188 --> 00:56:22,312
He’s really tough.

738
00:56:23,222 --> 00:56:26,400
Do you know the name of that woman
and where she lives?

739
00:56:27,805 --> 00:56:30,019
I heard her refer to herself as...

740
00:56:31,108 --> 00:56:31,866
Fah.

741
00:56:32,022 --> 00:56:35,500
Fah, something like that. I’m not sure,
but I don't know where she lives.

742
00:56:37,093 --> 00:56:37,851
Fah?

743
00:56:39,904 --> 00:56:40,906
Fah

744
00:56:42,049 --> 00:56:43,028
Fah.

745
00:56:44,925 --> 00:56:45,935
Sky.

746
00:57:05,763 --> 00:57:07,093
So,

747
00:57:07,828 --> 00:57:09,641
Sky really has a twin.

748
00:57:11,253 --> 00:57:12,575
How exciting!

749
00:57:13,276 --> 00:57:15,760
Sky has a twin who looks just like Sky.

750
00:57:16,472 --> 00:57:19,862
And Sky has a twin named Fah.

751
00:57:20,270 --> 00:57:22,925
S K Y Sky means Fah.

752
00:57:23,767 --> 00:57:25,855
Sky and Fah.

753
00:57:30,537 --> 00:57:31,409
Sorry, sir.

754
00:57:31,447 --> 00:57:31,912
Yes?

755
00:57:31,988 --> 00:57:33,699
Have you seen the person in this photo?

756
00:57:35,400 --> 00:57:36,426
No, I haven’t.

757
00:57:37,287 --> 00:57:38,213
Thank you.

758
00:57:46,960 --> 00:57:48,106
Excuse me, officer.

759
00:57:48,666 --> 00:57:50,548
Could Sky see, please?

760
00:57:54,384 --> 00:57:56,121
Sky wants to help you, officer.

761
00:57:57,680 --> 00:57:58,354
Sure.

762
00:59:07,889 --> 00:59:08,921
Excuse me.
